  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">A gene-specific variance-control approach corrects polygenicity-driven inflation observed in transcriptome-wide association studies (2026) in The American Journal of Human Genetics. Funding: Office of Science, NIAAA NIH HHS, National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases, National Cancer Institute Division of Cancer Prevention, University of Chicago.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">A gene-specific variance-control approach corrects polygenicity-driven inflation observed in transcriptome-wide association studies (2026) in The American Journal of Human Genetics is authored by Yanyu Liang, Festus M. Nyasimi and Hae Kyung Im. Topics: Inflation (cosmology), Genetic association, Econometrics, Association (psychology) and Regression.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">2 citations (OpenAlex). Citing venues include Journal of Allergy and Clinical Immunology and The American Journal of Human Genetics.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Limited online visibility beyond citations.</p>",
